 "version": 1,
 "note": "LIFE-865: who may call the two LIFE OS MCP servers (lifeos/buzz/mcp.py, lifeos.inbox.send_to_jim --mcp). `clients` map one trusted fact (the verified OAuth client, or the OS user of a stdio server) to a client id; a caller-supplied id, header, argument or environment variable is never read. `grants` are authorization_gate.Grant rows seeded only with what each client does today (reads for the two chat clients; no `send_to_jim` grant, because no client has that MCP server configured), each with an expiry; revoke = set `revoked` true. `policy` is the access_policy document they are checked against; its keys are fingerprints of the client ids, not secrets. Credentials are named, never held. Live proof per client and tool is on LIFE-877 (Nov 25 to 26 2026); a catalog row says `working` only where such a receipt exists. LIFE-873: `credentials` are scoped `lm1.<id>.<secret>` bearer credentials (Jim, Nov 22 2026, comments 13708): the service holds only the SHA-256 of the secret, never the secret; each names the one client it is and the existing Buzz identity it reads as (null = capabilities only). Read grants only; Personal only; expire 2027-02-22; revoke = set `revoked` true. LIFE-949 (Jim, Nov 23 and 24 2026): the five memory tools (store, recall, correct, revoke, ask) are granted to eight clients, Personal only, purpose personal-memory, real non-sensitive data, no expiry in practice (2099-12-31), revocable any time (set `revoked` true); the old synthetic-memory-test rows stay for tests but no tool uses that purpose now.",
